// std.collections — the Map and Set constructors (B2b design D3, ruling
// 2's shape: mapOf/setOf free functions, no Builder). The bodies are the
// keyed fictions: the checker walks them like any body, and codegen
// replaces each call site with the runtime entry. The generic clauses are
// the surface's own: K and V unify from the two lists' element types at
// the call, and the return application Map<K, V> / Set<T> is what the
// member face then reads. panic is the prelude's Never — it satisfies the
// return position without constructing a value no We source can name.
pub fn mapOf<K, V>(keys: List<K>, values: List<V>) -> Map<K, V> { panic("fiction") }
pub fn setOf<T>(items: List<T>) -> Set<T> { panic("fiction") }
